## Conclusion

The @slayzone/server extraction is **structurally complete**. Domain logic is pure, transport is injectable, CLI runs standalone, supervised embedded mode works, migration round-trip is wired. The remaining work is **operational + organizational**, not architectural:

- Auth + fallback UX are the only true blockers for shipping remote mode
- Feedback domain extraction + settings lazy-load are nice-to-haves
- Backup/export-import to server is its own scoped phase

**The hard work is done.** What's left is iteration on edges.
